# Tests in apps/lantern-garage/test/ that do NOT currently pass.
#
# Context: on 2026-08-18 this directory held 305 test files and CI ran FIVE of
# them, by explicit path. The other 300 had never run in CI at all — including
# every suite shipped with the 1.15.4 trader work. Measured that day: 279 pass,
# 26 do not. Wiring all 305 on at once would have produced a permanently-red
# job, which is how an alarm becomes background noise.
#
# So the 279 are enforced now and these 26 are quarantined WITH A RATCHET:
# scripts/run-garage-tests.mjs fails the build if a file listed here starts
# passing, so the list can only shrink. Delete a line when you fix its test.
#
# Known causes seen while triaging: some assert seed data that has since drifted
# (watchlist-store-seed), some depend on env this runner does not set. The 15
# jest-style suites (describe/expect with no jest installed) were brought onto
# node:test via test/_jest-compat.js on 2026-09-29 and removed from this list.
#
# exit-warnings: NOT a stale test. It pins P0-8 (never auto-confirm IBKR warnings on
# a BUY), and entries have passed acceptWarnings:true since 3aff30e2 (2026-08-10), so
# ibkr-cpapi confirms every warning type on entries. Leave it here until the trading
# lane narrows that change (e.g. benign-list the leveraged-ETF disclosure) or retires P0-8.
#
# 2026-10-11 — the thing that was BLOCKING that narrowing is fixed. placeOrder collected
# the warnings it cleared and then dropped them on the success path, so no auto-confirmed
# disclosure was ever recorded anywhere; BENIGN_WARNING_TEXT matches on WORDING, so the
# benign-list could not be written. A submitted order now reports `warnings` and
# `warningsConfirmed`. The next live entry that clears the leveraged/inverse-ETF notice
# records its exact text — at which point this becomes: add that one line to
# BENIGN_WARNING_TEXT, drop acceptWarnings from the two entry sites, and delete this
# entry. Still a FOUNDER call: it changes live order behaviour on an armed box, and
# getting it too narrow strands entries at needs_confirmation the way 2026-08-10 did.
exit-warnings.test.js

# `env:` entries are ENVIRONMENT-DEPENDENT, not broken, and are never ratcheted —
# their result is a property of the machine. These two pass on the 8GB dev box and
# fail on a hosted runner: they assert the on-box local-model setup (#2171 / #2173,
# qwen2.5-coder as the default local coding engine), which CI does not have.
# Ratcheting them would make the build red on whichever machine satisfies them,
# with no edit that satisfies both.
env: local-engine-qwen.test.js
env: local-model-registry.test.js
